<title>SINGAPORE: Malaysia cuts July term Tapis by 95 cts to $19.16.</title>
<headline>Malaysia cuts July term Tapis by 95 cts to $19.16.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysia's state-owned Petronas has lowered the July term lifting price of its Tapis crude oil by 95 cents per barrel to $19.16 from $20.11 in June, traders said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Petronas set the August alpha for Tapis at parity, from a 15-cent premium in July, traders said.</p>
<p>July Labuan was set at a fixed differential of Tapis plus 15 cents and Miri was set at Tapis plus 10 cents-unchanged from the previous month.</p>
<p>Bintulu differential was set at Tapis less 40 cents, also unchanged.</p>
<p>The price of July Dulang crude was set at $18.62 from $19.29 in June.</p>
<p>PETRONAS 1996/1997 TERM PRICES (INCLUDES ALPHA ADJUSTMENT)  </p>
<p>	    July    JUNE     MAY     APR     MAR     FEB     JAN</p>
<p>TAPIS    $19.16  $20.11   $21.30  $21.23  $22.39  $23.79  $26.23</p>
<p>LABUAN   $19.31  $20.26   $21.45  $21.38  $22.54  $23.94  $26.38</p>
<p>MIRI     $19.26  $20.21   $21.40  $21.33  $22.49  $23.89  $26.33</p>
<p>DULANG   $18.62  $19.29   $20.41  $20.35  $21.41  $23.08  $25.66</p>
<p>BINTULU  $18.76  $19.71   $20.90  $20.83  $21.89  $23.39  $25.83</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3082)</p>
